# Patent Claim Draft

**Title:** Medical Arm Support Device for Radial Access Procedures

---

## Claim 1

A medical arm support device for stabilizing a patient's arm during radial access procedures, comprising:

a) a base support member configured to be positioned beneath a patient's forearm, said base support member having a proximal end, a distal end, and an upper surface contoured to receive the forearm in an extended position;

b) a hand support component disposed at the distal end of the base support member, said hand support component comprising:
   - a palm-receiving surface configured to cradle the patient's hand in a supinated position;
   - a raised peripheral rim extending along at least a portion of the palm-receiving surface to inhibit lateral movement of the hand;
   - an adjustable wrist elevation feature configured to position the wrist in slight dorsiflexion to expose the radial artery access site;

c) at least one securing strap assembly comprising:
   - a first strap segment affixed to a first lateral edge of the base support member;
   - a second strap segment affixed to a second lateral edge of the base support member opposite the first lateral edge;
   - a hook-and-loop fastening interface disposed on facing surfaces of the first and second strap segments, configured to permit adjustable circumferential tightening about the forearm;
   - wherein the securing strap assembly is positioned proximal to the hand support component to immobilize the forearm while leaving the radial access site unobstructed;

d) a second securing strap configured to engage the hand support component and secure the patient's fingers or hand thereto, said second securing strap comprising a padded contact surface to minimize pressure-related discomfort during extended procedural durations;

e) wherein the base support member, hand support component, and securing strap assemblies cooperate to maintain the patient's wrist in a fixed position accessible to a clinician for insertion and manipulation of a radial access sheath.

---

## Claim 2 (Dependent)

The medical arm support device of claim 1, wherein the adjustable wrist elevation feature comprises an inflatable bladder disposed beneath the palm-receiving surface, said bladder being selectively inflatable to adjust the degree of wrist dorsiflexion.

## Claim 3 (Dependent)

The medical arm support device of claim 1, wherein the base support member further comprises a radiolucent material construction to permit unobstructed fluoroscopic imaging during the procedure.

## Claim 4 (Dependent)

The medical arm support device of claim 1, wherein the first and second strap segments each include a length-adjustment buckle to accommodate varying forearm circumferences.

## Claim 5 (Dependent)

The medical arm support device of claim 1, further comprising an armboard extension detachably coupled to the proximal end of the base support member, said armboard extension configured to support the upper arm and shoulder region of the patient.

---

